# SND project rules

## English identifiers only

All code identifiers must be in **English**. UI copy stays Serbian (latinica, ekavica); names in source code do not.

Applies to: variables, constants, functions, methods, parameters, props, types, interfaces, enums, class names, file names for modules/helpers, hook names.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
const infoPoruka = '...'
const jacinaLozinke = 'slaba'
function validirajEmail(v: string) {}
const [ucitavanje, setUcitavanje] = useState(false)
interface DugmeProps { punasirina?: boolean }

// ✅ GOOD
const infoMessage = '...'
const passwordStrength = 'weak'
function validateEmail(v: string) {}
const [loading, setLoading] = useState(false)
interface ButtonProps { fullWidth?: boolean }
```

Allowed Serbian:
- User-facing strings only (labels, errors, titles, aria-labels shown in UI)

CSS custom properties must be English (e.g. `--color-brand-500`, `--radius-md`).

Prefer clear English (`passwordStrength`, `formError`, `isLoading`) over transliteration.

---

## Icons

Use **lucide-react** for UI icons. Do not hand-draw SVG icons.

Keep custom SVG only for non-icon graphics (progress bars, avatars, illustrations).

```typescript
import { CircleCheckBigIcon, UserIcon } from 'lucide-react'

<CircleCheckBigIcon className="size-24" aria-hidden />
```

---

## File naming

Domain files use lowercase dotted names: `<name>.<kind>.ts`.

| Kind | File | Role |
|---|---|---|
| service | `auth.service.ts` | External I/O (Supabase, HTTP APIs) |
| query | `user.query.ts` | React Query keys for that domain |
| hooks | `auth.hooks.ts` | React Query hooks |
| helpers | `profile.helpers.ts` | Pure helpers (no I/O) |
| validation | `auth.validation.ts` | Input validation |
| types | `testimonials.types.ts` | Domain types |
| webhook | `didit.webhook.ts` | Webhook verify / parse |
| store | `kyc.store.ts` | Local/demo store |

Other descriptive kinds follow the same pattern (`profile.completeness.ts`, `query.client.ts`).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
authService.ts
useAuth.ts
queryKeys.ts
profileHelpers.ts

// ✅ GOOD
auth.service.ts
auth.hooks.ts
user.query.ts
profile.helpers.ts
```

Do **not** nest a `services/` or `queries/` folder. Put the file in `lib/<domain>/` or `hooks/<domain>/`.

React components stay PascalCase (`AddLocationForm.tsx`). ShadCN UI primitives stay kebab-case (`dropdown-menu.tsx`).

---

## Data layer architecture

```
Component → Hook (React Query) → Service (Supabase) → Database
```

Folder layout:
- `lib/<domain>/` — domain modules, including `.service.ts` and `.query.ts` (auth, user, profiles, …)
- `hooks/<domain>/` — `.hooks.ts` that call `lib/<domain>/` services
- `lib/query.client.ts` — QueryClient defaults
- `providers/QueryProvider.tsx` — wraps the app

Future domains get matching folders under both `lib/` and `hooks/` (items, bookings, messages).

Hard rules:
- Components **never** call Supabase or import `.service.ts` from `lib/`
- Components call **only** hooks from `hooks/`
- Hooks call **only** services from `lib/<domain>/`
- Services call **only** `lib/supabase/*` (or the domain's external API)
- Query keys always come from `lib/<domain>/*.query.ts` — never hardcode strings
- Cache updates via `queryClient.invalidateQueries` / `clear` — no ad-hoc refetch in components
- Session presence may still live in `context/AuthContext` for UI; mutations/queries go through hooks

```typescript
// ✅ Component
const signUp = useSignUp()
signUp.mutate({ email, password })

// ❌ Component
const supabase = createClient()
await supabase.auth.signUp(...)
```

---

## Server Components first

Pages and layouts stay **Server Components** by default. Do **not** add `'use client'` unless the file needs browser APIs: form state, event handlers, `useState` / `useEffect`, or React Query hooks.

React Query belongs in client islands (forms, mutations, live session UI) — not on whole pages that only render data.

If a page is mostly static, keep it a server component and extract the interactive bit into a small client child.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — whole page is a client bundle, no SSR for the shell
'use client'
export default function VerificationPage() {
  return <p>Identitet je potvrđen.</p>
}

// ✅ GOOD — server page
export default function VerificationPage() {
  return <p>Identitet je potvrđen.</p>
}

// ✅ GOOD — client only where interactivity lives
// page.tsx (server)
export default function LoginPage() {
  return <LoginForm />
}

// LoginForm.tsx
'use client'
export function LoginForm() {
  const signIn = useSignIn()
  // form state + mutate
}
```

Do not add `'use client'` just to use `Link`, `Image`, `className`, or lucide icons — those work in Server Components.
